# Pivot Exchange — observe three freely swinging physical pendulums.
# Copyright (c) 2026 Christian Ströbele (CrispStrobe). SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause.
# Freshly load either Pivot Exchange saved model before EVERY run.
# The saved 8-degree or 20-degree release angle is part of the real model placement.
# This program starts the lab and observes for 18 seconds. It has no motor commands.
# Compare the near and far suspension choices with the slow central-hole control.
DEVICE SPIKE
GLOBAL observing = 0
GLOBAL complete = 0
GLOBAL fault = 0
WHEN flag clicked:
  set observing to 0
  set complete to 0
  set fault to 0
  lab start
  IF (lab status) = "no-model" THEN:
    set fault to 1
    say "Freshly load a Pivot Exchange model, then run this observation program."
    stop all
  set observing to 1
  wait 18 seconds
  set observing to 0
  set complete to 1
  say "Observation complete. The two nearly conjugate suspensions should keep similar time; the central-hole control swings more slowly."
